# Windows Shell Safety

The default shell on this workspace is PowerShell. Avoid Bash-only command
syntax unless the command is explicitly executed through `sh`.

## PowerShell Sequencing

- Do not use `&&` or `||` in Shell commands.
- Use `; if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { ... } else { exit $LASTEXITCODE }`
  when the next command depends on the previous command succeeding.
- Use `;` only when later commands may run even if an earlier command fails.

## Heredocs And Commit Messages

When a heredoc is required, especially for `git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF' ...)"`,
pipe a PowerShell here-string into `sh` instead of nesting complex quotes inside
one command string:

```powershell
@'
set -e
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
docs(scope): concise message

EOF
)"
'@ | sh
```

## PATH Updates

After installing CLI tools with `winget` or `npm -g`, update `$env:Path` in the
current session before verifying the command. New terminals may not see PATH
changes until restarted.
